{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 77,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.77.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will cry unto God with my voice,\nEven unto God with my voice; and he will give ear unto me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.77.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In the day of my trouble I sought the Lord:\nMy hand was stretched out in the night, and slacked not;\nMy soul refused to be comforted.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.77.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I remember God, and am disquieted:\nI complain, and my spirit is overwhelmed. [Selah",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.77.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou holdest mine eyes watching:\nI am so troubled that I cannot speak.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.77.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have considered the days of old,\nThe years of ancient times.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.77.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I call to remembrance my song in the night:\nI commune with mine own heart;\nAnd my spirit maketh diligent search.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.77.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Will the Lord cast off for ever?\nAnd will he be favorable no more?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.77.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Is his lovingkindness clean gone for ever?\nDoth his promise fail for evermore?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.77.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hath God forgotten to be gracious?\nHath he in anger shut up his tender mercies? [Selah",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.77.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I said, This is my infirmity;",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "But I will remember",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the years of the right hand of the Most High.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.77.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will make mention of the deeds of Jehovah;\nFor I will remember thy wonders of old.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.77.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will meditate also upon all thy work,\nAnd muse on thy doings.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.77.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy way, O God, is in the sanctuary:\nWho is a great god like unto God?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.77.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou art the God that doest wonders:\nThou hast made known thy strength among the peoples.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.77.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast with thine arm redeemed thy people,\nThe sons of Jacob and Joseph. [Selah",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.77.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The waters saw thee, O God;\nThe waters saw thee, they were afraid:\nThe depths also trembled.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.77.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The clouds poured out water;\nThe skies sent out a sound:\nThine arrows also went abroad.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.77.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The voice of thy thunder was in the whirlwind;\nThe lightnings lightened the world:\nThe earth trembled and shook.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.77.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thy way was in the sea,\nAnd thy paths in the great waters,\nAnd thy footsteps were not known.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.77.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:PSA.77.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou leddest thy people like a flock,\nBy the hand of Moses and Aaron.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ],
  "headings": [
    {
      "style": "s1",
      "text": "Comfort in trouble from recalling God’s mighty deeds.",
      "before_verse": 1
    },
    {
      "style": "d",
      "text": "For the Chief Musician; after the manner of Jeduthun. A Psalm of Asaph.",
      "before_verse": 1
    }
  ]
}
